Patch 01: treat the app's own host as an app host, not a visitor custom domain.
Applies to: papermark/papermark main @ ed19717e, file middleware.ts

Why: upstream isCustomDomain() hardcodes papermark.com / papermark.io /
localhost / *.vercel.app. Any other host (including paper.woodwolfdigital.com)
is treated as a visitor custom link domain, so DomainMiddleware redirects "/"
to https://www.papermark.com and rewrites every other path to
/view/domains/<host><path>. The dashboard and login never render.
There is no env var to override this upstream (NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_BASE_HOST is
not read anywhere in the code), so the host must be exempted in code.

The exempt host is derived from NEXTAUTH_URL, which is already a required
env var. Note: middleware env is inlined at build time, so NEXTAUTH_URL
must be set as a Docker build arg as well as a runtime var (the Dockerfile
does this).
---
diff --git a/middleware.ts b/middleware.ts
--- a/middleware.ts
+++ b/middleware.ts
@@ -17,6 +17,23 @@ function isAnalyticsPath(path: string) {
 }
 
 function isCustomDomain(host: string) {
+  // Self-host: the app's own public host (from NEXTAUTH_URL) is not a
+  // visitor custom link domain. Upstream hardcodes papermark.com /
+  // papermark.io here, which makes every self-hosted domain fall into
+  // DomainMiddleware ("/" redirects to papermark.com, other paths rewrite
+  // to /view/domains/...). Exempt the app host so AppMiddleware runs.
+  const appHost = (() => {
+    try {
+      return new URL(
+        process.env.NEXTAUTH_URL || "https://paper.woodwolfdigital.com",
+      ).hostname;
+    } catch {
+      return "";
+    }
+  })();
+  if (appHost && host?.split(":")[0] === appHost) {
+    return false;
+  }
   return (
     (process.env.NODE_ENV === "development" &&
       (host?.includes(".local") || host?.includes("papermark.dev"))) ||
